*              gains optional columns and an optional delete action that the PAGE confirms (mode<2> to mode<4>, res 'delete').
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_pickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)
*
*   A THIN FACADE over $sl_picker, so that a page never names the library.  mode null: the person picks a file and then a record in it; 'file': only a file (id is null);
*   'record': file is given and only the record is picked.  res is 'ok' (file and id are the answer, with mode 'file' only file), 'new' (Ctrl-N in the list of records: file is the
*   file and newtext what had been typed into the filter; the page runs ITS OWN new-record path, with its own gates) or 'cancel' (Esc, a session with no terminal, no file to pick
*   from, or a file that cannot be opened).  THE PICKER NEVER WRITES: it opens the file for reading, takes no lock and creates, changes and deletes nothing; what the page does with
*   the answer, and whether it may, is the page's.  The window puts the screen back under it, so the page needs no redraw of its own.
*
*   mode 'list' (field 1; S.88 U9): a pick from a LIST THE PAGE GIVES, not from a file.  file = the entries, one to a field (value 1 the name, value 2 a description shown beside it,
*   value 3 the help shown on ?); id = the window's title on the way in and the number of the entry chosen (in file) on the way out; newtext = the number of the entry the window
*   starts on, on the way in, and null on the way out.  res is 'ok' (Enter chose) or 'cancel' (Esc, a session with no terminal, an empty list).  Typing narrows the list to the
*   entries that hold the text in the name, the description or a column.  Nothing is opened, read or written.  OPTIONAL (3 Nov 26, "Extend the picker"):
*     mode<2>  the column headings as values, the first for the name; an entry's value 2 then holds its column texts as subvalues
*     mode<3>  the column widths, as values, the same way
*     mode<4>  'delete': Del on an entry answers res 'delete' and id its number.  THE PICKER DELETES NOTHING: the page asks its own question (its box with the name typed,
*              Cancel the default) and deletes only on that answer.
*   The window is $sl_pickwin's; a page that passes none of mode<2> to mode<4> gets the window it always had.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_pickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)
$catalog $tk_pickrec

   call $sl_picker(mode, file, id, res, newtext)
   return
end

* END-CODE
